<title>UK: IMF gold sale plans irk world's big gold producers.</title>
<headline>IMF gold sale plans irk world's big gold producers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Big gold producers on Thursday said the International Monetary Fund's (IMF) plan to sell gold reserves was helping depress the price of gold bullion.</p>
<p>&quot;There is uncertainty hanging over the market right now as to what the IMF will do,&quot; said Sam Jonah, Chief Executive of Ashanti Goldfields Co Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Hopefully when the IMF uncertainty is removed, we would hope the fundamentals would take over and see an upturn in the gold prices,&quot; Jonah told Reuters at a gold conference sponsored by RBC Dominion Securities Inc.</p>
</text>
